 "title": "GS21 industry sign x standardized leverage (mean zero), BOUNDED y exposure (gs_bv_cap 2): six mirrored types on the gs_level ladder",
 "question": "gvyslz with the exposure bounded: does the product of the industry sign and the firm's standardized leverage give GS21 an interaction gap once every type has a finite equilibrium?",
 "notes": "WHY (2026-11-03). gvyslz's solves e and f (+0.2 at level 1.5, +0.35 at level 2.0) have no finite equilibrium: low-coupon firms in positive-loading industries carry exposure down to -0.28 / -0.48, pay most where the y discount is largest (My's diagonal 1.079 at the lowest node), and prices grow x1.065 a sweep (f: 1e128 at the cap). gs_bv_cap 2 (gs_solve_vy.py) replaces e^{e y} in production by h_e(y) = c / (1 + (c-1) e^{-c e y/(c-1)}), h(0) = 1, h'(0) = e, range (0, 2), kp_vy's bv_eps_cap one model over; the economy is otherwise gvyslz's. A 41-node test of f converged at sweep 3049 where the uncapped run diverged.\n\nPRECOMMITMENT STATUS: precommitted=false; ids filled from the Quest build log by the solve script before any seed runs.\n\nPREDICTION (2026-11-03): gvyslz's, room 30% or more and a fair gap at or above +0.029. FALSIFIED if room is at or below 10% on three seeds.",
